  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:veyitten_lekha_haelohim">
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/27/28"/><tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/1"/>And may God grant you
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/2"/>of the dew of heaven,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/3"/>and of the riches of the land,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/4"/>and an abundance of grain and wine.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/27/29"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/5"/>Peoples will serve you
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/6"/>and nations bow to you;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/7"/>be master over your brothers
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/8"/>and your mother's sons will bow to you.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/9"/>Those who curse you are cursed,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/10"/>and those who bless you, are blessed.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_1"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/28/3"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/11"/>May the Almighty, Shadai, bless you
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/12"/>and make you fruitful and multiply you,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/13"/>and you will become
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/14"/>a congregation of peoples.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/28/4"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/15"/>May He give you the blessing of Abraham,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/16"/>to you and to your descendants with you,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/17"/>that you inherit the land of your dwelling
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/18"/>which God gave to Abraham.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_2"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/49/25"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/19"/>From the Almighty of your father,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/20"/>And He will help you;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/21"/>and from Shadai, and He will bless you—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/22"/>the blessings of heaven above,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/23"/>the blessings of the deep that lie below,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/24"/>the blessings of breast and womb.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/49/26"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/25"/>The blessings of your father
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/26"/>have exceeded the blessings of my parents
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/27"/>to the utmost bounds of the eternal hills;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/28"/>—may they rest upon the head of Joseph,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/29"/>on the head [of the one]
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/30"/>separated from his brothers.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_3"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/7/13"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/31"/>He will love you and bless you
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/32"/>and multiply you;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/33"/>He will bless the fruit of your womb,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/34"/>and the fruit of your land—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/35"/>your grain, your wine, and your oil,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/36"/>the offspring of your cattle,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/37"/>and the flocks of your sheep,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/38"/>on the land
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/39"/>which He swore to your fathers,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/40"/>to give to you.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/7/14"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/41"/>Blessed will you be above all peoples;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/42"/>there will be among you no barren man
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/43"/>or barren woman,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/44"/>or among your livestock.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/7/15"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/45"/>Adonoy will remove from you all sickness,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/46"/>and all the severe illnesses of Egypt,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/47"/>which you know about,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/48"/>He will not set upon you
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/49"/>but will place them upon all who hate you.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_4"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/>
<tei:note type="description" xml:lang="en">The Blessing of Children</tei:note>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/48/16"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/50"/>The angel who redeems me from all evil,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/51"/>will bless the boys
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/52"/>and call upon them my name
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/53"/>and the name of my fathers,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/54"/>Abraham and Isaac,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/55"/>and like fish they will multiply
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/56"/>in the midst of the world.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_5"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/1/10"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/57"/>Adonoy, your God, has multiplied you,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/58"/>and you are today
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/59"/>like the stars of the sky, abundant.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/1/11"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/60"/>May Adonoy, God of your fathers,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/61"/>increase your present numbers
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/62"/>a thousandfold,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/63"/>and bless you as He has spoken to you.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_6"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/>
<tei:note type="description" xml:lang="en">The Blessing of Prosperity</tei:note>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/28/3"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/64"/>Blessed will you be in the city,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/65"/>and blessed will you be in the field.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/28/6"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/66"/>Blessed will you be upon entering
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/67"/>and blessed will you be upon leaving.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/28/5"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/68"/>Blessed is your basket
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/69"/>and your kneading-bowl.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/28/4"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/70"/>Blessed will be the fruit of your womb
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/71"/>and the fruit of your land;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/72"/>the fruit of your livestock,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/73"/>the offspring of your cattle
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/74"/>and the flocks of your sheep.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/28/8"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/75"/>Adonoy will command on your behalf
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/76"/>the blessing in your storehouses
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/77"/>and in everything
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/78"/>to which you put your hand;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/79"/>and He will bless you in the land
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/80"/>which Adonoy, your God, gives you.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/28/12"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/81"/>Adonoy will open for you
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/82"/>His good treasure—the heavens—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/83"/>to provide the rain of your land
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/84"/>in its proper time,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/85"/>and bless all the work of your hand;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/86"/>you will lend [to] many nations
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/87"/>but you will not borrow.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_7"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/15/6"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/88"/>For Adonoy, your God, has blessed you
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/89"/>as He has spoken to you;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/90"/>and you will make loans to many nations,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/91"/>but you will not need loans;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/92"/>you will rule many nations
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/93"/>but they will not rule you.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_8"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/33/29"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/94"/>Fortunate [are you,] Israel; who is like you—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/95"/>a people delivered by Adonoy—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/96"/>Who is your helping shield
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/97"/>and the sword of Your pride;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/98"/>your enemies will try to deceive you
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/99"/>but you will tread on their high places.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_9"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/>
<tei:note type="description" xml:lang="en">Blessing of Redemption</tei:note>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/44/22"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/100"/>I have blotted out
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/101"/>your transgressions like a mist,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/102"/>and your sins like a cloud;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/103"/>return to Me for I have redeemed you.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/44/23"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/104"/>Sing joyously heavens,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/105"/>for Adonoy has made [you],
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/106"/>shout for joy, depths of the earth.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/107"/>Burst out, mountains, in joyous song,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/108"/>forest and every tree therein—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/109"/>for Adonoy has redeemed Jacob
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/110"/>and through Israel He will be glorified.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/111"/>Our Redeemer—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/112"/>Adonoy of Hosts is His Name,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/113"/>the Holy One of Israel.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_10"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:note type="description" xml:lang="en">Blessing of Deliverance</tei:note>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/45/17"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/114"/>Israel will be delivered by Adonoy
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/115"/>[for] an everlasting deliverance;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/116"/>you will not be shamed or humiliated
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/117"/>for all eternity.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_11"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:joel/2/26"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/118"/>You will eat and be satisfied,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/119"/>and will praise
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/120"/>the Name of Adonoy, your God,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/121"/>Who has dealt with you wondrously;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/122"/>and My people will never be ashamed.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:joel/2/27"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/123"/>And you will know
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/124"/>that in the midst of Israel am I;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/125"/>I am Adonoy, your God,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/126"/>there is no other;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/127"/>and My people will never be ashamed.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_12"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/55/12"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/128"/>For in joy will you go out [of exile]
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/129"/>and in peace
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/130"/>will you be brought [homeward],
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/131"/>the mountains and the hills
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/132"/>will burst out before you in joyous song,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/133"/>and all the trees of the field
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/134"/>will clap hands.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_13"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/12/2"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/135"/>Behold the Almighty is my deliverance;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/136"/>I am secure and will not fear,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/137"/>for the strength and retribution
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/138"/>of Yah, Adonoy
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/139"/>was the cause of my deliverance.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/12/3"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/140"/>And you will draw water with gladness,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/141"/>from the wellsprings of the deliverance.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/12/4"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/142"/>And you will say on that day—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/143"/>give thanks to Adonoy, proclaim His Name,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/144"/>make known His ways among the peoples;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/145"/>cause it to be mentioned
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/146"/>that His Name is exalted.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/12/5"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/147"/>Sing to Adonoy
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/148"/>for glorious things has He done,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/149"/>this is known throughout the earth.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/12/6"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/150"/>Jubilate and sing joyously, dweller in Zion,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/151"/>for great in your midst
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/152"/>is the Holy One of Israel.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_14"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/25/9"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/153"/>And it will be said on that day,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/154"/>‘Behold, this our God,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/155"/>we have hoped for Him
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/156"/>and He delivered us;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/157"/>this is Adonoy for Him, we have hoped.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/158"/>We will exult and rejoice
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/159"/>in His deliverance.'<tei:anchor xml:id="note_15"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/>
<tei:note type="description" xml:lang="en">Blessing of Relief, Rescue and Joy</tei:note>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/2/5"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/160"/>House of Jacob,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/161"/>go forth, let us walk in the light of Adonoy.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_16"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/33/6"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/162"/>The trust of your times
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/163"/>the strength of [all] deliverances
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/164"/>[will be] wisdom and perception—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/165"/>the fear of Adonoy is their protection.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_17"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:samuel_1/18/14"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/166"/>And David was successful in all his ways,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/167"/>and Adonoy was with him.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_18"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/55/19"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/168"/>He redeemed my soul in peace
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/169"/>from the battle that threatened me
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/170"/>because many were with me.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_19"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:samuel_1/14/45"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/171"/>And the people said to Saul,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/172"/>“Shall Jonathan die,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/173"/>who has achieved
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/174"/>this great deliverance
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/175"/>in Israel?
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/176"/>Far be it!
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/177"/>As Adonoy lives,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/178"/>not a hair of his head will fall
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/179"/>to the ground!
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/180"/>For with the help of God
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/181"/>did he accomplish [it] this day.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/182"/>And the people redeemed Jonathan,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/183"/>and he did not die.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_20"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/184"/>Those redeemed by Adonoy will return
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/185"/>and come to Zion with joyous song
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/186"/>and everlasting joy on their heads;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/187"/>gladness and joy will they attain,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/188"/>and sorrow and grief will flee.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_21"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/189"/>You have turned my mourning into dancing
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/190"/>You have loosened my sackcloth
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/191"/>and supported me with joy.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_22"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/23/6"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/192"/>And Adonoy your God would not consent
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/193"/>to heed Bilaam;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/194"/>and Adonoy, your God, turned for you
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/195"/>the curse into a blessing,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/196"/>for Adonoy, your God, loves you.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_23"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:jeremiah/31/13"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/197"/>Then the maiden will rejoice in dance,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/198"/>young men and elders [will dance] together;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/199"/>I will turn their mourning into gladness,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/200"/>I will comfort them and provide them joy
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/201"/>from their sorrow.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_24"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/>
<tei:note type="description" xml:lang="en">Blessing of Peace</tei:note>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/57/19"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/202"/>The Creator of the speech of the lips [says]:
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/203"/>“Peace, peace, to him who is far
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/204"/>and to him who is near”;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/205"/>Adonoy says—“and I will heal him.”<tei:anchor xml:id="note_25"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:chronicles_1/12/19"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/206"/>A spirit enwrapped Amassai,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/207"/>the chief of the captains,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/208"/>“We are yours, David,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/209"/>we are with you, son of Yishai;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/210"/>peace, peace to you,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/211"/>and peace to your helpers;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/212"/>for God has helped you.”
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/213"/>And David accepted them,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/214"/>and placed them at the heads of the troop.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_26"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:samuel_1/25/6"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/215"/>And you will say,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/216"/>“Let it be so with the living!
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/217"/>May you be at peace
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/218"/>and your household at peace,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/219"/>and all that is yours at peace.”<tei:anchor xml:id="note_27"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/220"/>Adonoy will grant strength to His people,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/221"/>Adonoy will bless His people with peace.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_28"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/222"/>Rabbi Yochanan said:
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/223"/>“Wherever you find
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/224"/>the greatness of the Holy One, blessed is He,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/225"/>there you will find His humility.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/226"/>This is written in the Torah,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/227"/>reiterated in the Prophets
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/228"/>and stated a third time in the [Holy] Writings.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/229"/>It is Written in the Torah:
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/10/17"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/230"/>“For Adonoy, your God,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/231"/>He is the God of gods,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/232"/>and Master of masters,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/233"/>the Almighty,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/234"/>the Great, the Powerful, the Awesome,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/235"/>Who has no regard for personages
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/236"/>and takes no bribes.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/237"/>And following it is written:
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/10/18"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/238"/>“He does justice for the orphan and widow,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/239"/>and loves the stranger,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/240"/>giving him food and clothing.”<tei:anchor xml:id="note_29"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/241"/>It is reiterated in the Prophets,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/242"/>where it is written:
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/57/15"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/243"/>“Thus says He Who is exalted uplifted,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/244"/>He Who dwells eternally,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/245"/>and holy is His Name,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/246"/>in the exalted and holy [place] I dwell—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/247"/>and with the contrite and humble of spirit,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/248"/>to revive the spirit of the humble
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/249"/>and to revive the heart of the contrite.”<tei:anchor xml:id="note_30"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/250"/>And a third time in the [Holy] Writings
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/251"/>as it is written:
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/252"/>“Sing to God, compose hymns to His Name,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/253"/>extol Him Who rides over the heavens,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/254"/>with His Name, Yah,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/255"/>and exult before Him.”
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/256"/>And thereafter it is written:
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/68/6"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/257"/>“The Father of orphans and Judge of widows,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/258"/>is God, in His holy dwelling.”
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:kings_1/8/57"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/259"/>May Adonoy, our God, be with us
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/260"/>as He was with our fathers,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/261"/>may He never abandon us or cast us off.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_31"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/262"/>And you who hold fast to Adonoy, your God,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/263"/>are all alive today.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_32"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/51/3"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/264"/>For Adonoy comforts Zion,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/265"/>He comforts all of her ruins,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/266"/>He will make her wilderness like Eden,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/267"/>and her desolate places
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/268"/>like a garden of Adonoy;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/269"/>gladness and joy will be found there—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/270"/>thanksgiving and the sound of song.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_33"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/271"/>Adonoy desired
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/272"/>for the sake of His righteousness
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/273"/>to make the Torah great and to glorify it.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_34"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/128/1"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/274"/>A song of ascents.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/275"/>Fortunate is everyone who fears Adonoy,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/276"/>who walks in His ways.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/128/2"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/277"/>The toil of your hands,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/278"/>when you eat thereof—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/279"/>fortunate are you, good will be yours.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/128/3"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/280"/>Your wife is a fruitful vine
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/281"/>in the innermost parts of your home,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/282"/>your children are like olive plants
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/283"/>around your table.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/128/4"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/284"/>Behold, so is blessed the man
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/285"/>who fears Adonoy.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/128/5"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/286"/>May Adonoy bless you out of Zion,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/287"/>and may you look upon the good of Jerusalem
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/288"/>all the days of your life.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/128/6"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/289"/>May you see [the] children of your childrn,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:veyitten_lekha_haelohim/290"/>peace upon Israel.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_35"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/></tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
